17592186299661 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105703 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299662 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105703 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299663 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105703 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186339003 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105703 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186374538 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105703 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387678 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105703 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441581 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105703 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186441588 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105703 #edb/ref 1039 "Perpendicular Vectors" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105703 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186105480 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105703 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "84c96375-27d5-5ada-a952-34e09b3e92bf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105967 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106562 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105967 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106563 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105967 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106564 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105967 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106565 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105967 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106566 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105967 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106567 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105967 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106650 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105967 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105967 #edb/ref 1045 "Calculating a Vector Projection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105967 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186106562 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105967 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050394 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105967 #edb/ref 1050 840.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105967 #edb/ref 1050 840.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186105967 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "a038488b-d4de-5f2b-9c61-0a4bc91a3757" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106111 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186102542 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106111 #edb/ref 1069 "q-19219" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106111 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that $\\mid a|= 8$, $\\mid b|= 2$ and that the angle between the vectors is $θ = 120^{∘}$. Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b$ in terms of the vector $b$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106111 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "923b55ee-6062-5c44-a28a-51ce2a7ca4a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106172 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186290105 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106172 #edb/ref 1069 "q-212461" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106172 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106172 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ x\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106172 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "88b493a3-ac09-5d83-bae2-26aab369c0d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106172 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =-4\\cdot 4+4\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot x \\\\  & =x-20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ x-20 & =0 \\\\ x & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106562 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106650 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106562 #edb/ref 1061 121755 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106562 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "26031206-512a-5b41-90d5-299987889655" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106562 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186107166 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106563 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106564 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106563 #edb/ref 1061 121756 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106563 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e6fd410f-37e5-5a4e-a29d-c160c7d2a397" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106563 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105701 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106564 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106565 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106564 #edb/ref 1061 121759 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106564 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a78e2420-8af1-50c7-9a19-b4ceac9bcde4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106564 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186107167 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106565 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106567 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106565 #edb/ref 1061 121760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106565 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "af715941-1577-597e-b254-6bc4aa300b8f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106565 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105702 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106566 #edb/ref 1061 121763 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106566 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "146819e4-ecad-5e47-8884-a05b59624d07" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106566 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105703 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106567 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106566 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106567 #edb/ref 1061 121766 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106567 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ec38d18e-577a-5ebc-8349-60991ef75b80" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106567 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186107168 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106650 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106563 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106650 #edb/ref 1061 187844 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106650 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fdc39c18-bf51-5a32-a828-404d1e341f7a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106650 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186107181 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107166 #edb/ref 1064 "The **vector projection** of a vector $\\mathbf{a}$ onto another vector $\\mathbf{b}$ is the portion that the vector $\\mathbf{a}$ extends along $\\mathbf{b}.$\n\nFor example, consider two vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ shown below. Suppose we know that $|\\mathbf{a}|=2,$ $|\\mathbf{b}|=3,$ and the angle between the vectors is $\\theta = \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}.$\n\n![](images/a2/a28278cf12885ab7f845407ac2fa7f4ffa00dbe30849a3f8ff41f02e134ed3a0.png)\n\nThe starting point of the vector projection is $O,$ and the ending point will be the point $P$ that lies on the line containing $\\mathbf{b}$ with $AP \\perp \\mathbf{b},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/f0/f0b267fb009e79eb16f86be42edc2c835808b28aa3eaf1c7e857300224ee01ec.png)\n\nThe vector $\\overrightarrow{OP}$ is called the **vector projection** of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}.$ It is denoted as $\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}}\\,\\mathbf{a},$ and it is computed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =OP\\cdot u \\\\  & ={\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a\\cdot u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\text{comp}_{\\mathbf{b}}\\,\\mathbf{a} = |\\,\\mathbf{a}\\,| \\cos\\theta$ is the scalar projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{u}$ is a unit vector in the direction of $\\mathbf{b}.$\n\nFirst, we compute the scalar projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =|\\,a\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{b}}{|\\,\\mathbf{b}\\,|} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{b}}{3} = \\dfrac{1}{3} \\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & ={\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a\\cdot u \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}b \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107166 #edb/ref 1065 9051 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107166 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "5962a19e-bb12-54d8-b53a-24578711fa53" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107166 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107167 #edb/ref 1064 "We have been using the following formula for the vector projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\text{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}}\\,\\mathbf{a} =\\text{comp}_{\\mathbf{b}}\\,\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{u}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can write an alternative formula using the formula for the scalar projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,b\\,|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the original formula for the vector projection, and also substituting $\\mathbf{u} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{b}}{| \\, \\mathbf{b} \\, |},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,b\\,|}\\cdot \\frac{b}{|\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,b\\,{|}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, another general formula for the vector projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107167 #edb/ref 1065 9052 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107167 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "e4098700-6d5c-5618-90a8-8dea2d4dbed0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107167 #edb/ref 1067 "A General Formula" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107168 #edb/ref 1064 "Notice that if two vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are perpendicular, then by projecting $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$ (or $\\mathbf{b}$ onto $\\mathbf{a}$), we obtain the zero vector.\n\nFor example, the projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto a perpendicular vector $\\mathbf{b}$ looks as follows:\n\n![](images/91/9163eda36b752f1e36195b8b5a1d40bf545ec21a3988f5480d6ddcbb926c00ea.png)\n\nFurthermore, we have the following fact:\n\n*If $\\mathbf{a}$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $\\mathbf{b}$ equals the zero vector if and only if the vectors are perpendicular.*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107168 #edb/ref 1065 9059 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107168 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "97117437-4034-5cb8-84a6-675d75d4f874" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107168 #edb/ref 1067 "Projecting Perpendicular Vectors" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107181 #edb/ref 1064 "When finding the projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b},$ we sometimes find that the resulting projection vector points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{b}.$ This happens when the vector $\\mathbf{a}$ extends in the direction opposite to that of $\\mathbf{b}.$\n\n![](images/0e/0e973e6f6484a9aad863ebfe89fc1ea6356d6a50844931306c6aa2b63be18a8a.png)\n\nConsider two vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b},$ where it is known that \n\n$$\n|\\,\\mathbf{a}\\,|=2,\\qquad |\\,\\mathbf{b}\\,|=3,\\qquad \\theta = 135^\\circ.\n$$\n\nLet's calculate $\\textrm{proj}_{\\mathbf{b}}\\,\\mathbf{a}.$ \n\nFirst, notice that the angle between $\\mathbf a$ and $\\mathbf b$ is obtuse. This means we expect the projection vector to point in the opposite direction to that of $\\mathbf b.$\n\nNext, we compute the scalar projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =|\\,a\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡({135}^{∘}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the scalar projection is negative. \n\nThen, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{b}}{|\\,\\mathbf{b}\\,|} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{b}}{3} = \\dfrac{1}{3} \\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & ={\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a\\cdot u \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis vector points in the direction opposite to $\\mathbf{b},$ as expected." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107181 #edb/ref 1065 9677 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107181 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "2df5fde5-316c-5962-8f0d-56362287c447" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107181 #edb/ref 1067 "The Direction of the Projection Vector" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186235874 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨0,\\frac{2}{13},\\frac{3}{13}⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186235874 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186235874 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0b320351-bc5f-5d30-8e1b-115490175e6d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236077 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨0,\\frac{2}{73},\\frac{3}{73}⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236077 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236077 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "29861cc0-282e-55e8-bb73-6b1c84f3194b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236186 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨0,0,0⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236186 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236186 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3aa6322d-6e21-5ba1-8a56-0d7256be7736" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236603 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨0,\\frac{4}{13},\\frac{6}{13}⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236603 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236603 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7ec4107b-3b2f-5d39-9dc6-6d7a9eda213d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236671 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨0,\\frac{4}{73},\\frac{6}{73}⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236671 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236671 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "88a89953-8437-5bb0-bfe1-f370c45a6462" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237579 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186235874 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237579 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186236077 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237579 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186236186 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237579 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186236603 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237579 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186236671 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237579 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237579 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237579 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186236603 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237579 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6b5736ba-ea23-5e79-9cac-607c5a0cd1a0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237848 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186237579 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237848 #edb/ref 1069 "q-101541" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237848 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237848 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237848 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9c17c0ad-57b9-5e4e-96cf-a2591d364b0a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237848 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\cdot 0+7\\cdot 2+(-4)\\cdot 3}{{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{13}⟨0,2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\frac{4}{13},\\frac{6}{13}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285488 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨-\\frac{7}{9},\\frac{2}{9},-\\frac{1}{9}⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285488 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285488 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4b553699-5a2a-55ea-a60a-4950dd9ea937" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285767 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨0,0,0⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285767 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285767 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6ac1aeed-3d56-5091-b3b9-4d438a865c4c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286194 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨-\\frac{7}{54},\\frac{2}{9},-\\frac{1}{54}⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286194 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286194 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "99864ad9-d222-5dec-953f-0ff7b38374cf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286608 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨\\frac{2}{9},-\\frac{7